---
description: Remove what a removed path leaves behind; no switch that switches nothing
alwaysApply: true
---

# No dead code

When a path is removed, remove in the same change everything that only served it: functions, methods, parameters threaded through callers, fields, flags, constants, tests, rustdoc, and the design and README text.

Do not keep a public API that has no effect "for compatibility". The crate is unpublished (`version = "0.0.0"`, `publish = false`), so there is no caller to keep compatible. When it is published, compatibility is decided by a design Issue, not assumed.

A function under `#[cfg(test)]` stays only while a test calls it. An independent reference that a numeric test compares against (`.cursor/rules/numeric-tests.mdc`) is such a caller.

```text
# BAD: the parallel build is gone, the flag stays
pub fn parallel(self, enable: bool) -> Self { let _ = enable; self }

# GOOD: the flag goes with the build it selected, with its tests and docs
(no parallel() on any builder; it returns with a parallel build, through a Grill)
```
